ld like to  ask tab what is it that as you look back  at this remarkable journey that we've  all just experienced again with you  watching it  what is it personally professionally  forget you know  No Limits that you feel proud as tough  as you look back well I would say the  wonderful people that I've worked with I  mean they're the contributors there  those are the ones that you feed from  and you hopefully can give them back to  all that they're giving you when you're  working with them I mean how could I  ever not acknowledge you having worked  with look  you know Visconti or or or John  Frankenheimer Arthur Penn Sidney Lumet's  I mean you know some radiant Phil  Carlson bill Wellman I mean really great  great people I've been very fortunate  and the actors and actresses I can't I  can't forget about them and Geraldine  page said something to me one time I was  working with her and I said God Jerry  you know everyone loves you the press  hate my guts and she said she grabs a  lot of my armors to remember this tab if  people don't like you that's their bad  taste I thought wow that's pretty nice  so I thought you know I'm gonna apply  that to my life and furthermore I look  out at everybody and I say look just  remember people don't like you that's  their problem not yours
 

